---
import "../styles/global.css";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

export const prerender = false;
---

<!doctype html>
<html class="light" lang="en">
<head>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
<link
href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Outlined:opsz,wght,FILL,GRAD@20..48,100..700,0..1,-50..200"
rel="stylesheet"
/>
<link
href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=Geist:wght@400;600;700;800&display=swap"
rel="stylesheet"
/>

<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" name="viewport" />
<title>Sky States Channel Partners | The Team Behind the Training</title>
<meta
name="description"
content="Meet the partners powering Sky States from behind the scenes, DC Technology, Scube Technology, and Shefsolutions llc, and see how they turn training into real careers."
/>
<link rel="canonical" href="https://skystates.us/channel-partners" />
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />

<style>
.material-symbols-outlined {
  font-variation-settings:
  "FILL" 0,
  "wght" 400,
  "GRAD" 0,
  "opsz" 24;
}
.mesh-gradient {
  background: radial-gradient(at top right, rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.15) 0%, transparent 50%),
  radial-gradient(at bottom left, rgba(2, 132, 199, 0.08) 0%, transparent 50%),
  linear-gradient(180deg, #f8fafc 0%, #ffffff 100%);
}
</style>
</head>
<body class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 font-sans overflow-x-hidden antialiased">
<Header />

<main class="w-full -mb-24">
<!-- Hero Section -->
<section class="relative w-full pt-20 pb-5 md: md:pb-6 overflow-hidden mesh-gradient">
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 md:px-12 relative z-10 text-center flex flex-col items-center gap-4">

<div class="inline-block px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-sky-100 border border-sky-200 text-[11px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-900 mt-4 shadow-sm">
Our Channel Partners
</div>

<h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
The Network Behind the Name
</h1>

<p class="text-sm md:text-base text-slate-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
A bootcamp is only as good as what happens after graduation day. These are the partners who make sure "job-ready" actually means job-ready.
</p>

</div>
</section>

<!-- Intro Section -->
<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 md:px-12 py-3 md:py-5">
<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-5 md:p-6 shadow-sm border border-slate-200 text-center">
<p class="text-sm md:text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
Here's a truth most bootcamps won't say out loud: certificates don't get people hired. Networks do. Real projects do. A machine that actually runs behind the curtain does. So instead of pretending Sky States does it all solo, we'll introduce you to the crew that makes the whole thing work.
</p>
</div>
</section>

<!-- Partners Grid -->
<section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 md:px-12 py-4">
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 lg:gap-6">

<!-- DC Technology -->
<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm border border-slate-200 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow relative overflow-hidden group">
<div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-1 bg-sky-500"></div>
<div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-sky-50 text-sky-600 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-xl">work</span>
</div>
<div class="mb-3">
<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">DC Technology</h3>
<span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-sky-600 uppercase tracking-wide">Staffing Partner</span>
</div>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-sm text-justify">
Finishing a program is one thing. Getting a recruiter to actually call you back is another game entirely, and that's where DC Technology comes in. As our staffing partner, they're the connective tissue between "I just built a portfolio" and "I just got an offer." When a Sky States graduate is ready to step into the job market, DC Technology's network is part of what makes that step land somewhere real instead of into a black hole of unanswered applications.
</p>
</div>

<!-- Scube Technology -->
<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm border border-slate-200 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow relative overflow-hidden group">
<div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-1 bg-emerald-500"></div>
<div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-600 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-xl">architecture</span>
</div>
<div class="mb-3">
<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Scube Technology</h3>
<span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-emerald-600 uppercase tracking-wide">Project Partner</span>
</div>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-sm text-justify">
Nobody gets hired for acing a quiz. They get hired for proving they can build something that actually works under real conditions. Scube Technology is our project partner, and their fingerprints are all over the hands-on, industry-grade work our students tackle during the program. Think less "textbook exercise," more "the kind of problem you'd actually get handed in your first month on the job." That difference matters more than most people realize until they're sitting in an interview trying to talk about it.
</p>
</div>

<!-- Shefsolutions llc -->
<div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm border border-slate-200 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow relative overflow-hidden group">
<div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-1 bg-amber-500"></div>
<div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 text-amber-600 flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-xl">settings_suggest</span>
</div>
<div class="mb-3">
<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Shefsolutions llc</h3>
<span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-amber-600 uppercase tracking-wide">Delivery Partner</span>
</div>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-sm text-justify">
Every great classroom experience has an invisible engine keeping it running on time, on track, and without the chaos students never even see. That's Shefsolutions llc's job as our delivery partner. Sessions starting when they're supposed to, cohorts moving in sync, the operational gears turning quietly in the background, that's them. It's the least glamorous part of the story and one of the most important.
</p>
</div>

</div>
</section>

<!-- Why This Matters Section -->
<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 md:px-12 py-8 mt-4">
<div class="space-y-4 text-center">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Why This Actually Matters</h2>
<p class="text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
Anyone can slap "career support" on a landing page. Fewer can back it up with an actual staffing pipeline, real project partnerships, and the operational muscle to deliver a program that doesn't fall apart by week three. That's the difference between a promise and infrastructure, and it's exactly what this partner network represents.
</p>
</div>
</section>

<!-- Want In? CTA Section -->
<section class="w-full bg-slate-100 py-10 md:py-12 mt-4 border-t border-slate-200/60">
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 md:px-12 text-center space-y-5">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Want In?</h2>
<p class="text-sm md:text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto">
Sky States is always looking to grow this network further. If your organization does staffing, project delivery, or program execution and you want to be part of turning learners into hires, let's talk.
</p>

<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4 pt-2">
<a href="mailto:info@skystates.us" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-700 bg-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all font-semibold">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sky-600 text-[20px]">mail</span>
info@skystates.us
</a>
<a href="mailto:support@skystates.us" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-700 bg-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all font-semibold">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sky-600 text-[20px]">support_agent</span>
support@skystates.us
</a>
<a href="tel:8888102434" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-700 bg-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all font-semibold">
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-sky-600 text-[20px]">phone</span>
(888) 810-2434
</a>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</main>

<Footer />
</body>
</html>
